IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-actors`

-- ccc30-forms-warrants.l4 -- FORM 7, 7.1, 8, 16, 16.1 and 19 to 23 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (raw text lines 18015-18072, 18346-18374 and 18403-18462):
-- the warrant for arrest, the warrant to enter a dwelling-house, the warrant for committal, the subpoena to a witness and the warrants of remand and committal.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- WHAT IS A RULE HERE. The identification blocks, recitals and signature lines are prescribed wording; so are the commands to the officers (the warrant is the instrument that
-- orders them). What is encoded is what the Forms say beyond their wording: the grounds the Forms list with the sections each cites (a table, Forms 7, 7.1 and 8); the limit on entering a
-- dwelling-house (Form 7); what a keeper is to do and what ends it (Forms 8, 19 to 23: "until ...", "unless ... paid sooner"); the witness's duty to attend and what the subpoena says of records
-- (Forms 16 and 16.1, including the definitions of "record" and "therapeutic record" that Form 16.1 quotes from section 278.1).
-- NAMES. Form 16.1 quotes definitions that section 278.1 gives; they are encoded here as `form 16.1 ...` names, what the FORM says, so that they can never meet another part's `s 278.1 ...` names.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). Every JUST FALSE branch carries a FALSE-kind comment that quotes the words;
-- every NOTHING branch carries a NOTHING-kind comment. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Forms 7 to 23 -- the vocabulary the warrants share`

-- A section number as a decimal and a subsection as the Code writes it (a local helper: this module does not import the register).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      ss IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`forms 7 to 23 the provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF n, ss

DECLARE `forms 7 to 23 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 7 arrests the accused and brings them before the court, judge or justice named in the warrant`
    `form 8 receives the accused into custody in the prison`
    `form 16 attends before the court or justice, gives evidence and brings the things specified`

§ `Form 7 -- Warrant for arrest`

-- "And because (check those that are applicable): (a) ... (j) (if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant)."
-- Each ground carries, in brackets, the sections the Form itself cites for it (parsed from the text). The list of grounds is not closed (paragraph (j) takes any other statutory ground),
-- so a ground outside (a) to (i) is not covered; this table answers only which sections the Form cites for a ground.
DECLARE `form 7 ground` IS ONE OF

    `form 7 ground (a)`
    `form 7 ground (b)`
    `form 7 ground (c)`
    `form 7 ground (d)`
    `form 7 ground (e)`
    `form 7 ground (f)`
    `form 7 ground (g)`
    `form 7 ground (h)`
    `form 7 ground (i)`
    `form 7 ground (j)`

-- src:18023 | □ (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue this warrant for the arrest of the accused [507(4), 512(1)];
-- src:18024 | □ (b) the accused failed to attend court in accordance with the summons served on the accused [512(2)];
-- src:18025 | □ (c) (an appearance notice or undertaking) was confirmed and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with it [512(2)];
-- src:18026 | □ (d) it appears that a summons cannot be served because the accused is evading service [512(2)];
-- src:18027 | □ (e) the accused was ordered to be present at the hearing of an application for a review of an order made by a justice and did not attend the hearing [520(5), 521(5)];
-- src:18028 | □ (f) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or is about to contravene the (summons or appearance notice or undertaking or release order) on which the accused was released [512.3];
-- src:18029 | □ (g) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has committed an indictable offence since their release from custody on (summons or appearance notice or undertaking or release order) [512.3];
-- src:18030 | □ (h) the accused was required by (appearance notice or undertaking or summons) to attend at a time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and did not appear at that time and place [512.1, 512.2];
-- src:18031 | □ (i) an indictment has been found against the accused and the accused has not appeared or remained in attendance before the court for their trial [597];
-- src:18032 | □ (j) (if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant).
@ref Form 7 (Sections 475, 493, 597, 800 and 803) Warrant for Arrest, the grounds and the sections cited (src:18023-18032)
GIVEN ground IS A `form 7 ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Provision of the Code`)
`form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `form 7 ground (a)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 507 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512 "(1)")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (b)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512 "(2)")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (c)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512 "(2)")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (d)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512 "(2)")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (e)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 520 "(5)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 521 "(5)")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (f)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512.3 "")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (g)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512.3 "")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (h)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512.1 "", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 512.2 "")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (i)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 597 "")
    WHEN `form 7 ground (j)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant)"

-- "(Check if applicable) Because there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is or will be present in (specify dwelling-house), this warrant is also issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house
-- for the purpose of arresting the accused, subject to the condition that you may not enter the dwelling-house unless you have, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to believe that the
-- person to be arrested is present in the dwelling-house."
-- Not checked: the grant ("this warrant is also issued to authorize you to enter") is not in the warrant, a grant limited by its own wording, so the case is outside it (NOTHING: fork F-V; not an express no).
-- Checked: "you may not enter ... unless you have, immediately before entering ..., reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is present" (a flat negative with an "unless"):
-- without that belief JUST FALSE, with it JUST TRUE.
-- src:18034 | □ (Check if applicable) Because there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is or will be present in (specify dwelling-house), this warrant is also issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting the accused, subject to the condition that you may not enter the dwelling-house unless you have, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is present in the dwelling-house.
@ref Form 7 (Sections 475, 493, 597, 800 and 803) Warrant for Arrest, entry into the dwelling-house (src:18034)
GIVEN `the dwelling-house box is checked on the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before entering, the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is present in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the dwelling-house box is checked on the warrant`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this warrant is also issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting the accused"
        IF NOT `immediately before entering, the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is present in the dwelling-house`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "you may not enter the dwelling-house unless you have, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is present in the dwelling-house"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "Therefore, you are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to immediately arrest the accused and to bring them before (state court, judge or justice), to be dealt with according to law."
-- The warrant's own command to the peace officers. No time is stated beyond "immediately", which is not a number, so the rule has no WITHIN.
-- src:18033 | Therefore, you are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to immediately arrest the accused and to bring them before (state court, judge or justice), to be dealt with according to law.
@ref Form 7 (Sections 475, 493, 597, 800 and 803) Warrant for Arrest, the command (src:18033)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 7 to 23 action`
`form 7 the peace officers must arrest the accused and bring them before the court, judge or justice` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 7 arrests the accused and brings them before the court, judge or justice named in the warrant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer`
         BECAUSE "Form 7: the accused was not arrested and brought before the court, judge or justice named in the warrant"

§ `Form 7.1 -- Warrant to enter a dwelling-house`

DECLARE `form 7.1 ground` IS ONE OF
    `form 7.1 ground (a)`
    `form 7.1 ground (b)`
    `form 7.1 ground (c)`

-- "Whereas there are reasonable grounds to believe: (a) a warrant referred to in this or any other Act of Parliament to arrest or apprehend the person is in force anywhere in Canada; (b) grounds exist to arrest the
-- person without warrant under paragraph 495(1)(a) or (b) or section 672.91 of the Criminal Code; or (c) grounds exist to arrest or apprehend without warrant the person under an Act of Parliament, other than this Act;"
-- The sections the Form itself names inside a ground: paragraph (b) names paragraphs 495(1)(a) and (b) and section 672.91; paragraphs (a) and (c) name none of this Act's sections.
-- src:18046 | (a) a warrant referred to in this or any other Act of Parliament to arrest or apprehend the person is in force anywhere in Canada;
-- src:18047 | (b) grounds exist to arrest the person without warrant under paragraph 495(1)(a) or (b) or section 672.91 of the Criminal Code; or
-- src:18048 | (c) grounds exist to arrest or apprehend without warrant the person under an Act of Parliament, other than this Act;
@ref Form 7.1 (Section 529.1) Warrant To Enter Dwelling-house, the grounds and the sections named (src:18046-18048)
GIVEN ground IS A `form 7.1 ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Provision of the Code`)
`form 7.1 the sections the Form names in the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `form 7.1 ground (a)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the ground names no section of this Act ("this or any other Act of Parliament")
    WHEN `form 7.1 ground (b)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 495 "(1)(a)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 495 "(1)(b)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 672.91 "")
    WHEN `form 7.1 ground (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the ground names no section of this Act ("an Act of Parliament, other than this Act")

-- "This warrant is issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person." The authority is limited by its own wording: the dwelling-house
-- described and the purpose stated. Entry for another purpose, or into another dwelling-house, is outside it (NOTHING), not an express no.
-- src:18049 | And whereas there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person is or will be present in (here describe dwelling-house);
-- src:18050 | This warrant is issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person.
@ref Form 7.1 (Section 529.1) Warrant To Enter Dwelling-house, the authority to enter (src:18049-18050)
GIVEN `the dwelling-house is the one described in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 7.1 the warrant authorizes the officer to enter the dwelling-house` MEANS
    IF `the dwelling-house is the one described in the warrant` AND `the entry is for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person"

§ `Form 8 -- Warrant for committal`

DECLARE `form 8 ground` IS ONE OF

    `form 8 ground (a)`
    `form 8 ground (b)`
    `form 8 ground (c)`
    `form 8 ground (d)`
    `form 8 ground (e)`
    `form 8 ground (f)`

-- "And because (check those that are applicable): (a) ... (f) (if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant)."
-- The sections the Form cites in brackets for each ground (parsed from the text). Paragraph (b) carries an asterisk in this text: the footnote it points to is not in the converter's output (NOTES.md finding).

-- src:18062 | □ (a) the prosecutor has shown cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified [515(5)];
-- src:18063 | □ (b) a release order has been issued but the accused has not yet complied with the conditions of the order [519(1), 520(9), 521(10), 524(8), 525(6)];*
-- src:18064 | □ (c) the application by the prosecutor for a review of the release order has been allowed and that release order has been vacated, and the prosecutor has shown cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified [521];
-- src:18065 | □ (d) the accused has contravened or was about to contravene a (summons or appearance notice or undertaking or release order) and it was cancelled, and the detention of the accused in custody is justified [515(10), 523.1(3), 524(3), (4) and (6.2)];
-- src:18066 | □ (e) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has committed an offence after having become subject to the (summons or appearance notice or undertaking or release order) and the detention of the accused in custody is justified [515(10), 524(3), (4) and (6.2)];
-- src:18067 | □ (f) (if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant).
@ref Form 8 (Sections 493 and 515) Warrant for Committal, the grounds and the sections cited (src:18062-18067)
GIVEN ground IS A `form 8 ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Provision of the Code`)
`form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `form 8 ground (a)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 515 "(5)")
    WHEN `form 8 ground (b)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 519 "(1)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 520 "(9)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 521 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(8)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 525 "(6)")
    WHEN `form 8 ground (c)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 521 "")
    WHEN `form 8 ground (d)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 515 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 523.1 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(6.2)")
    WHEN `form 8 ground (e)` THEN JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 515 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 the provision` 524 "(6.2)")
    WHEN `form 8 ground (f)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant)"

-- "You are ordered to receive the accused in your custody in this prison and keep them safely there until they are delivered by due course of law."
-- An "until" bar: the keeper is to keep the accused (JUST TRUE) until they are delivered by due course of law (JUST FALSE from then).
-- src:18069 | You are ordered to receive the accused in your custody in this prison and keep them safely there until they are delivered by due course of law.
@ref Form 8 (Sections 493 and 515) Warrant for Committal, the keeper's order (src:18069)
GIVEN `the accused has been delivered by due course of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 8 the keeper is to keep the accused in custody in the prison` MEANS
    IF `the accused has been delivered by due course of law`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are delivered by due course of law"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:18068 | Therefore, you are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to arrest the accused and convey them safely to the (prison) at , and there deliver them to its keeper, with the following order:
-- src:18069 | You are ordered to receive the accused in your custody in this prison and keep them safely there until they are delivered by due course of law.
@ref Form 8 (Sections 493 and 515) Warrant for Committal, the keeper's order (src:18068-18069)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 7 to 23 action`
`form 8 the keeper must receive the accused into custody` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `form 8 receives the accused into custody in the prison`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the keeper of a prison`
         BECAUSE "Form 8: the accused was not received into custody in the prison"

§ `Form 16 -- Subpoena to a witness`

-- "This is therefore to command you to attend before (set out court or justice), on the day of A.D. , at o’clock in the noon at to give evidence concerning the said charge.* and to bring with you anything in your
-- possession or under your control that relates to the said charge, and more particularly the following: (specify any documents, objects or other things required)."
-- The asterisk after "charge." points to a footnote that is not in this text (NOTES.md finding). The days until the day set out are the input.
-- src:18352 | This is therefore to command you to attend before (set out court or justice), on the day of A.D. , at o’clock in the noon at to give evidence concerning the said charge.*
-- src:18353 | and to bring with you anything in your possession or under your control that relates to the said charge, and more particularly the following: (specify any documents, objects or other things required).
@ref Form 16 (Section 699) Subpoena to a Witness, the command (src:18352-18353)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the subpoena` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 7 to 23 action`
`form 16 the witness must attend and give evidence` MEANS
    PARTY `a witness`
    MUST `form 16 attends before the court or justice, gives evidence and brings the things specified`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the subpoena`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a witness`
         BECAUSE "Form 16: the witness did not attend before the court or justice on the day, at the time and at the place stated"

§ `Form 16.1 -- Subpoena to a witness: proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection 278.11(1)`

DECLARE `form 16.1 act the subpoena speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `form 16.1 bring the things specified to the court on the date and at the time indicated`
    `form 16.1 provide the things specified to a person`
    `form 16.1 discuss the contents of the things specified with a person`
    `form 16.1 do anything else`

-- "You are only required to bring the things specified above to the court on the date and at the time indicated, and you are not required to provide the things specified to any person or to discuss their
-- contents with any person unless and until ordered by the court to do so."
-- "only required to bring": anything else is JUST FALSE. "not required ... unless and until ordered": JUST FALSE until the court orders; once it has ordered, the sentence says no more (NOTHING: NOTES.md F-B).
-- src:18366 | You are only required to bring the things specified above to the court on the date and at the time indicated, and you are not required to provide the things specified to any person or to discuss their contents with any person unless and until ordered by the court to do so.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, take note: what the witness is required to do (src:18366)
GIVEN act IS A `form 16.1 act the subpoena speaks of`
      `the court has ordered the witness to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 the witness is required to` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `form 16.1 bring the things specified to the court on the date and at the time indicated` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 16.1 provide the things specified to a person`
        THEN IF `the court has ordered the witness to do so`
             THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless and until ordered by the court to do so": the exception is met and the sentence says no more
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "you are not required to provide the things specified to any person"
    WHEN `form 16.1 discuss the contents of the things specified with a person`
        THEN IF `the court has ordered the witness to do so`
             THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless and until ordered by the court to do so": the exception is met and the sentence says no more
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or to discuss their contents with any person"
    WHEN `form 16.1 do anything else` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You are only required to bring the things specified above to the court on the date and at the time indicated"

-- "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, it may be subject to a determination by the court in accordance with sections
-- 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code as to whether and to what extent it should be produced."
-- src:18367 | If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, it may be subject to a determination by the court in accordance with sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code as to whether and to what extent it should be produced.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, take note: a determination by the court (src:18367)
GIVEN `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 the thing may be subject to a determination by the court` MEANS
    IF `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record"

-- "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record ..., the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code, this subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of an
-- application for the production of the record or therapeutic record made under section 278.12 of the Criminal Code, and you will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production ..."
-- src:18368 | If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code, this subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of an application for the production of the record or therapeutic record made under section 278.12 of the Criminal Code, and you will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production of the record or therapeutic record.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, take note: the application and the opportunity to make submissions (src:18368)
GIVEN `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 the subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of the application made under section 278.12` MEANS
    IF `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code"

-- src:18368 | If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code, this subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of an application for the production of the record or therapeutic record made under section 278.12 of the Criminal Code, and you will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production of the record or therapeutic record.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, take note: the application and the opportunity to make submissions (src:18368)
GIVEN `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 the witness will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production` MEANS
    IF `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code"

-- "... you are not required to bring it with you until a determination is made in accordance with those sections as to whether and to what extent it should be produced."
-- The bar "the witness is not yet required to bring it" is JUST TRUE before the determination and JUST FALSE after it (the "until" ruling); a thing outside sections 278.1 to 278.19 is outside the sentence.
-- src:18369 | If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code, you are not required to bring it with you until a determination is made in accordance with those sections as to whether and to what extent it should be produced.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, take note: not required to bring it until a determination (src:18369)
GIVEN `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a determination has been made in accordance with those sections as to whether and to what extent it should be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 the witness is not yet required to bring the record or therapeutic record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing specified is a record or therapeutic record the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record, as those terms are defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 of the Criminal Code"
        IF `a determination has been made in accordance with those sections as to whether and to what extent it should be produced`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until a determination is made in accordance with those sections as to whether and to what extent it should be produced"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `form 16.1 kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `form 16.1 a medical record`
    `form 16.1 an education record`
    `form 16.1 an employment record`
    `form 16.1 a child welfare record`
    `form 16.1 an adoption record`
    `form 16.1 a social services record`
    `form 16.1 a personal journal or diary`
    `form 16.1 a record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature`
    `form 16.1 none of those kinds`

-- "As defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy and includes medical, education,
-- employment, child welfare, adoption and social services records, personal journals and diaries, and any record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of
-- Parliament or a provincial legislature, but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence."
-- A flat exclusion first ("does not include"). Then "means ... and includes ...", read as closed: the means limb plus the listed extension (a marginal reading, as in the keel); outside both is JUST FALSE.
-- src:18370 | As defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy and includes medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption and social services records, personal journals and diaries, and any record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature, but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, the definition of record quoted from section 278.1 (src:18370)
GIVEN `the record contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `form 16.1 kind of record`
      `the record was made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the record was made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
        IF `the record contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (kind EQUALS `form 16.1 none of those kinds`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy"

-- "As defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling
-- provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling."
-- src:18371 | As defined in section 278.1 of the Criminal Code, therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling.
@ref Form 16.1 (Subsections 278.12(5) and 699(7)) Subpoena to a Witness, the definition of therapeutic record quoted from section 278.1 (src:18371)
GIVEN `the record was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` MEANS
    IF `the record was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling`
       AND `it was provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling"

§ `Form 19 -- Warrant remanding a prisoner`

-- "And you, the keeper of the prison, are directed to receive each of the persons into your custody in the prison and keep each person safely until the day when that person’s remand expires and then to have that
-- person before me or any other justice on (date), at (hour), at (place), there to answer to the charge and to be dealt with according to law, unless you are otherwise directed before that time."
-- Two bars on keeping: "until the day when that person’s remand expires" and "unless you are otherwise directed before that time".
-- src:18410 | And you, the keeper of the prison, are directed to receive each of the persons into your custody in the prison and keep each person safely until the day when that person’s remand expires and then to have that person before me or any other justice (or if the signatory is not the justice, before any justice) on (date), at (hour), at (place), there to answer to the charge and to be dealt with according to law, unless you are otherwise directed before that time.
@ref Form 19 (Sections 516 and 537) Warrant Remanding a Prisoner, the keeper's direction (src:18410)
GIVEN `the day when the person's remand expires has come` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the keeper has been otherwise directed before that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 19 the keeper is to keep the person safely in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the keeper has been otherwise directed before that time`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless you are otherwise directed before that time"
        IF `the day when the person's remand expires has come`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the day when that person’s remand expires"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 20 -- Warrant of committal of a witness for refusing to be sworn or to give evidence`

-- "You, the keeper, are directed to receive the witness into your custody in the prison and safely keep them there for the term of days, unless they sooner consent to do what was required of them, and for so doing
-- this is a sufficient warrant."  The term is a number of days the justice fills in: the caller says whether it has run.
-- src:18422 | You, the keeper, are directed to receive the witness into your custody in the prison and safely keep them there for the term of days, unless they sooner consent to do what was required of them, and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant.
@ref Form 20 (Section 545) Warrant of Committal of Witness for Refusing to Be Sworn or to Give Evidence, the keeper's precept (src:18422)
GIVEN `the term of days has run` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness has consented to do what was required of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 20 the keeper is to keep the witness safely in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the witness has consented to do what was required of them`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they sooner consent to do what was required of them"
        IF `the term of days has run`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the term of days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 21 -- Warrant of committal on conviction`

-- "... to imprison him or her there for the term(s) of his or her imprisonment, unless, if a term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs, those amounts and the costs and charges of
-- the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison are paid sooner, and this is a sufficient warrant for so doing."
-- The "unless" operates only for a term imposed only in default of payment. Then payment of "those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison" ends the keeper's authority (JUST FALSE).
-- src:18437 | You are hereby commanded, in Her Majesty’s name, to arrest the offender if it is necessary to do so in order to take the offender into custody, and to take and convey him or her safely to (prison) at and deliver him or her to its keeper, who is hereby commanded to receive the accused into custody and to imprison him or her there for the term(s) of his or her imprisonment, unless, if a term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs, those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison are paid sooner, and this is a sufficient warrant for so doing.
@ref Form 21 (Sections 570 and 806) Warrant of Committal on Conviction, the keeper's precept (src:18437)
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs`
       AND `those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison have been paid`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, if a term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs, those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the offender to that prison are paid sooner"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 22 -- Warrant of committal on an order for the payment of money`

-- "You, the keeper of the prison, are directed to receive the defendant into your custody in this prison and keep them safely there for the term of , unless the amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of
-- conveying the defendant to the prison are sooner paid, and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant."
-- src:18448 | You, the keeper of the prison, are directed to receive the defendant into your custody in this prison and keep them safely there for the term of , unless the amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defendant to the prison are sooner paid, and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant.
@ref Form 22 (Section 806) Warrant of Committal on an Order for the Payment of Money, the keeper's precept (src:18448)
GIVEN `the amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defendant to the prison have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term has run` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 22 the keeper is to keep the defendant safely in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defendant to the prison have been paid`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defendant to the prison are sooner paid"
        IF `the term has run`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the term of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 23 -- Warrant of committal for failure to furnish a recognizance to keep the peace`

-- "You, the said keeper, are hereby commanded to receive the accused into your custody in the said prison and imprison him there until he enters into a recognizance as aforesaid or until he is discharged in due course of law."
-- src:18459 | You, the said keeper, are hereby commanded to receive the accused into your custody in the said prison and imprison him there until he enters into a recognizance as aforesaid or until he is discharged in due course of law.
@ref Form 23 (Sections 83.3, 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2) Warrant of Committal for Failure To Furnish Recognizance To Keep the Peace, the keeper's precept (src:18459)
GIVEN `the accused has entered into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been discharged in due course of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused has entered into the recognizance` OR `the accused has been discharged in due course of law`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until he enters into a recognizance as aforesaid or until he is discharged in due course of law"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

